+## Falsifiability (verified this leg, not committed)
+
+A throwaway harness loaded a deliberately broken `app.js` (rebuilds the list on every completion
+toggle). All three watchbill scenarios went red:
+- `Completing a todo keeps the same element in the DOM` -- held reference detached (rebuilt list).
+- `Uncompleting a todo keeps the same element in the DOM` -- same.
+- `@conformance ...` -- structural check caught `completeTodo` rebuilding via `renderList()` on a
+  same-visibility path.
+The out-of-scope `Editing a todo hides its label` stayed green, confirming the watchbill scopes to the
+two acceptance failures only.
+
+Against the current repo build (`js/app.js` already carries the in-place mutation), all four
+dom-stability scenarios pass. So the specs are calibrated: red on the defective build the acceptance
+suite exercises, green on the fixed build.
 
